{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1535105-hsien-and-demons","id":1535105,"title":"Hsien and Demons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-03T09:38:55-07:00","id":1535105,"title":"Hsien and Demons","content":"How do you handle the similarities between Hsien and Fallen?<br /> The stories of servants of Heaven exiled as punishment by the ruler of heaven and forced to inhabit soulless human bodies as they decide wether to work at going back to Heaven or make their own way should make for interesting crossovers.<br /> Would the August Personnage of Jade be the same god as the god of the Fallen? Would the Fallen recognize the Shinma as long lost parents?<br /> Would the Hsien find kinship with the Demons or would they be horrified to see these dark mirrors of themselves? Could they see the Fallen as their own form of Thallain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-03T18:32:44-07:00","id":1535121,"title":"","content":"My headcanon is that the Hsien are effectively Angels, and that is that. They're the same class of being, but working under a different punishment altogether, which makes for their difference in mechanics.<br /> <br /> I also have other things and Kiths as the actual Changelings from Asia, when that's relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-03T20:14:37-07:00","id":1535123,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve always felt that the August Personage of Jade and God from Demon the Fallen were the same person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 05-03-2024, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-03T21:01:30-07:00","id":1535127,"title":"","content":"Not a direct answer but it may be interesting to those who like/are interested in the little gods:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/changeling-the-dreaming-in-the-realm-of-gods-and-dreams-live-drafting-a-hsien-reboot.911145/\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre...reboot.911145/</a><br /> <br /> this is a thread of a really cool revamp of the little gods as a concept. If you like this the thread author also did one for the Kuei-Jin. YMMV of course, but I found it super interesting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-03T21:15:03-07:00","id":1535129,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Hsien are far more analogous to the Fallen than to any other group, and if you're looking to put The Land of Eight Million Dreams together with Demon: the Fallen, it's very easy to just say that the August Personage of Jade and God are the same being, that the Yama Kings were demons in Lucifer's retinue, and the Hsien are Angels given a unique punishment for their decision to remain neutral and not join Heaven's side.<br /> <br /> If you want to keep them separate, that's possible too. Keep in mind that the Hsien are divided into three groups. There are those still loyal to Heaven who, through their reincarnations, due their best to follow Heaven's laws and seek forgiveness for their original sins. Then there are those who have given up and have become selfish and corrupt. They don't believe that they will ever be forgiven so they do their best to enjoy their lives as they can. And then there are the ones who have fully embraced corruption and joined the Yama Kings. They serve as mercenaries in their armies, and between incarnations are rewarded by being sent to the Hell of Pleasure. So the attitude of a given Hsien towards one of the Fallen would heavily depend on which faction they're in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T06:34:55-07:00","id":1535260,"title":"","content":"I did not know about the Hsien, but will look into them further; I suspect the magic system from Changeling might be a satisfactory substitute for the rather busted system of spells and powers Fallen get. At a glance, their origin story bears so much resemblance to that of the Fallen that I think, yeah, they're the same creatures.<br /> <br /> Off topic, but it's long been my headcanon that the Wan Xian were the Malhim before they fell from grace and became vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T14:09:50-07:00","id":1535301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1535105-hsien-and-demons?p=1535260#post1535260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did not know about the Hsien, but will look into them further; I suspect the magic system from Changeling might be a satisfactory substitute for the rather busted system of spells and powers Fallen get. At a glance, their origin story bears so much resemblance to that of the Fallen that I think, yeah, they're the same creatures.<br /> <br /> Off topic, but it's long been my headcanon that the Wan Xian were the Malhim before they fell from grace and became vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hsien have always been a stranger in Changeling, with their origin and everything about them having nothing to do with the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> But they fit Demon just perfectly. And you can easily place their origin as a &quot;second Fall&quot; of sorts, it's just that their crime was punished differently. Which makes perfect sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T14:07:35-07:00","id":1535463,"title":"","content":"Another interesting note is how Hsien are closer mechanically to Dark Age era Fae(who were confirmed ancestors of the changelings in the darkening skies supplement), and the Dark Age fallen are much closer mechanically to DA fae(The need to balance Conviction and Torment is like how Fae/Hsien need to balance Mist and Weaving/Yang and Yin, demons also gain physical features when raising torment in a similar to, but very distinct system from, how Fae raising their mists gain New Mein features).<br /> <br /> It's actually possible that Fae and Angel might have some kind of common metaphysical ancestor like how living animals have common evolutionary ancestors.<br /> <br /> Another interesting fact is that DA Fae are born from a race of spirits called &quot;sprites&quot;, which are spirits in the WTA/MTA sense with a Gnosis/Rage/Willpower stat spread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-12T13:12:56-07:00","id":1535491,"title":"","content":"I didn't know there were playable Fallen in the Dark Age setting! Which book(s) are they in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-12T13:32:06-07:00","id":1535496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1535105-hsien-and-demons?p=1535491#post1535491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't know there were playable Fallen in the Dark Age setting! Which book(s) are they in?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember the name right now, but it is a Vampire supplement, with very different rules. Many find them best than the rules of DtF, I strongly disagree.<br /> <br /> Either way, lore-wise there's not really a change in rules, it's just a gameline thing. If you want to play DA Demon, they're very few and directly summoned by someone, as Hell is still closed, so there's little to no society of theirs outside the minions of the Earthbound.<br /> <br /> Going by the methods and description, you can expect those Demons to have higher Torment too, but no hard rules on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-12T16:16:09-07:00","id":1535498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1535105-hsien-and-demons?p=1535491#post1535491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't know there were playable Fallen in the Dark Age setting! Which book(s) are they in?</div> </div> </div> </div>The book is called &quot;Devil's Due&quot;. The fallen in the DA time period were generally Much weaker than modern fallen, generally worse at gaining faith and unable to access their lores until more modern days, but they had better grip on their torment and could use it access more of their apocalyptic form powers than modern fallen(modern fallen have 16 form points total, DA fallen could have 100+ depending on torment).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-12T19:28:52-07:00","id":1535500,"title":"","content":"As I said, Devil's Due is a Vampire supplement. While you can interpret its rules as &quot;DA Demon&quot;, they're actually rules to play a demon compatible with the narrative and mechanical role they have in Vampire, and that's why it doesn't use any of the rules from DtF even when copying one trait or another.<br /> <br /> But that said, I do suggest reading it. The rules are quite different and more to the taste of some people, even if not mine. My point is that this difference does not represent an actual difference in the fiction, so whatever set of rules you prefer, you can use for a game at any point in time, be them Devil's Due's, DtF's or a blend of both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-13T04:06:47-07:00","id":1535507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1535105-hsien-and-demons?p=1535500#post1535500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said, Devil's Due is a Vampire supplement. While you can interpret its rules as &quot;DA Demon&quot;, they're actually rules to play a demon compatible with the narrative and mechanical role they have in Vampire, and that's why it doesn't use any of the rules from DtF even when copying one trait or another.<br /> <br /> But that said, I do suggest reading it. The rules are quite different and more to the taste of some people, even if not mine. My point is that this difference does not represent an actual difference in the fiction, so whatever set of rules you prefer, you can use for a game at any point in time, be them Devil's Due's, DtF's or a blend of both.</div> </div> </div> </div>It kind of does represent DA DtF Demons though.<br /> <br /> It's explained in the &quot;Ritual of Sundered Soul&quot; side-box that this is representative of DtF demons at the time. The mechanical differences are explicitly because of the constant background radiation of hostile True Faith caused by the rise of Christianity conquering europe. The mechanics are the to represent demons at the weakest they've ever been.<br /> <br /> So it's not accurate to just call it a &quot;Vampire supplement&quot; and dismiss it like when splats represent other splats in the back of their corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-13T13:50:23-07:00","id":1535526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1535105-hsien-and-demons?p=1535507#post1535507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It kind of does represent DA DtF Demons though.<br /> <br /> It's explained in the &quot;Ritual of Sundered Soul&quot; side-box that this is representative of DtF demons at the time. The mechanical differences are explicitly because of the constant background radiation of hostile True Faith caused by the rise of Christianity conquering europe. The mechanics are the to represent demons at the weakest they've ever been.<br /> <br /> So it's not accurate to just call it a &quot;Vampire supplement&quot; and dismiss it like when splats represent other splats in the back of their corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of does isn't the same as does, but let me explain.<br /> <br /> As far as lore and fluff goes, DD is, indeed, representative of Demons in the DA. That does includes the design goal of the rules, in this case weaker demons, is DtF canon. It is also relevant in that it is the only Vampire supplement about infernalism whose demons are specifically the Fallen.<br /> <br /> But the rules are still made as an extension of VtM rules, not as an extension of DtF rules. It is clear by the style of said rules, specially for Pacts and Apocalyptic Form.<br /> <br /> While a lot of people like those rules more than DtF's, Devil's Due is not a reboot of DtF rules and isn't meant to be an official DA Demon, just the closer to it they were going to make at that point in time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T01:13:45-07:00","id":1536146,"title":"","content":"Tangentially, if Hsien count as fallen angels would a Hsien's child be a Kinain or a Nephilim/Laham?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T13:01:30-07:00","id":1536164,"title":"","content":"Probably a human, actually, but possibly a Nephilim. Even by RAW there's no indication that they produce Kinain, and going by the similarity with the Fallen, there's no reason to even consider it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-02T11:58:57-07:00","id":1536707,"title":"","content":"I don't feel the Hsien are actually adjacent to Demons. They can go back into the Umbra and the August Courts. They are more akin to the demigods and demihumans of Chinese, Indian and Southeast Asian mythology and work differently to the Fallen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-02T13:30:00-07:00","id":1536711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1535105-hsien-and-demons?p=1536707#post1536707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't feel the Hsien are actually adjacent to Demons. They can go back into the Umbra and the August Courts. They are more akin to the demigods and demihumans of Chinese, Indian and Southeast Asian mythology and work differently to the Fallen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Despite only referring to the spirit world as the place ghosts go, there's sufficient evidence to conclude this is a narrative choice and not some restriction on umbral travel for the Fallen, and they did visit the Silver Citadel (which is currently empty).<br /> <br /> That they work differently to the Fallen and are similar to Eastern entities is a given. They're a completely different set of rules meant for interaction with Changeling, and based, well, on Asian minor gods.<br /> <br /> But we're discussing a more interesting way of using them than what canon gives us.<br /> <br /> Hsien aren't needed overall. Asian legends are mostly well covered by the same rules for umbral entities and other stuff that cover entities and creatures from any other culture. On top of that, they're not meant to cover those things, they're specifically meant to cover minor gods, specially (though not exclusively) as seen under the structure of the Celestial Bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> And they're very specifically meant to be their own thing on this, not any other kind of creature. This is not just a matter of mechanics, but their unique lore.<br /> <br /> So the point here is, &quot;pairing&quot; them with Demon, or rather assuming some link, some adjacency to Angels, makes more sense than their current link to the Dreaming, which is just weird and out of place. It also justify their existence as their thing.<br /> <br /> In this case, the Hsien can be a narrative foil to the Fallen as servants of a similar Creator (that may or may not be the same one), with a similar role (maybe or maybe not being originally the same type of creature), and a similar state as sinners/rebels, but whose crimes are distinct, with opposite punishment (isolation from Creation and humans vs binding to Creation and humans) and circumstances (bound to humans by God's command vs bound to humans as an act of rebellion). If they're really Angels or whatever is completely irrelevant and probably unknowable.<br /> <br /> Other than that they become another case of orientalism like the other Asian splats, something actual Asian players already complained repeatedly including in this very Forum. It's a splat that exists to be the same but Asian and so not the same because Asian, for no other reason than say that things are different and more Wuxia in Asia.<br /> <br /> We have here an interesting splat, but made for all the wrong reasons, and maybe the most egregious in this. We can give it a new, better reason to exist, one that lets Asia also have the usual splats without stepping on their toes. Or we can just let it go. They don't really add anything worthy to the setting and narrative otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T09:21:43-07:00","id":1536750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1535105-hsien-and-demons?p=1536711#post1536711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hsien aren't needed overall. Asian legends are mostly well covered by the same rules for umbral entities and other stuff that cover entities and creatures from any other culture. On top of that, they're not meant to cover those things, they're specifically meant to cover minor gods, specially (though not exclusively) as seen under the structure of the Celestial Bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> And they're very specifically meant to be their own thing on this, not any other kind of creature. This is not just a matter of mechanics, but their unique lore.<br /> <br /> So the point here is, &quot;pairing&quot; them with Demon, or rather assuming some link, some adjacency to Angels, makes more sense than their current link to the Dreaming, which is just weird and out of place. It also justify their existence as their thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>And here, you lose me. The link to the Changeling is the problem in itself. It's not the solution to just paste them onto another splat with a completely different narrative purpose and a design.You'd do the same error of false equivalency and &quot;our splats are different&quot; they did when they introduced them initially.<br /> <br /> The Value of Hsien is the fact that they represent a different kind of stories and different kind of myths. Those myths are better represented by them being their own thing. This has been treated way more interestingly by Hsienfan on rpg.net who did the excellent revision of KotE as well.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T16:44:34-07:00","id":1536767,"title":"","content":"Do you have a link to this revision?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T17:36:54-07:00","id":1536774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1535105-hsien-and-demons?p=1536767#post1536767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have a link to this revision?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/changeling-the-dreaming-in-the-realm-of-gods-and-dreams-live-drafting-a-hsien-reboot.911145/\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre...reboot.911145/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T17:17:38-07:00","id":1536822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1535105-hsien-and-demons?p=1536774#post1536774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/changeling-the-dreaming-in-the-realm-of-gods-and-dreams-live-drafting-a-hsien-reboot.911145/\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre...reboot.911145/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>72 pages of thread is a lot, but it seems that it will be released as a book, did I understood right? It does seem to have been a very good project, and it had the approval of some people whose opinions I respect a lot (which does include you).<br /> <br /> It seems, though, that a lot of people there still saw the Hsien as adjacent to the Fallen to some degree, although maybe not in the same way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-05T14:57:44-07:00","id":1536848,"title":"","content":"Well. Someone saw some links, but neither the author nor the general sentiment of the thread was about embracing Demon for the treatment of Hsien. It's a long thread and it's essentially open development of a sourcebook, so you can see the author's thoughts and how they develop their ideas for the Splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-05T19:32:28-07:00","id":1536858,"title":"","content":"Oh, I'm not saying it was embracing Demon. Some of the comments go the other way around, bringing Demon closer to Changeling. I don't know, I didn't see much, but the author seemed to agree on <i>some</i> link between them.<br /> <br /> Neither here or there, though. I still think the link with Demon proposed in this thread is the way to go without recreating the splat from zero, along with having the actual fae from Asia with the treatment for new Kiths from C20.<br /> <br /> But that thread goes for the whole creation from scratch path and I do want to either read the book if it becomes one, or eventually read the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}